            <ArticleTitle>Safety profile of treatment in diabetic peripheral neuropathic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S43-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>New treatment options for diabetic peripheral neuropathic pain (DPNP) have recently been developed, including two Food and Drug Administration (FDA) approved agents, duloxetine and pregabalin. As clinicians face a broader spectrum of efficacious treatments, side-effect profiles play an increasingly important role in the development of a pain management regimen. In this article we review the safety profile of agents commonly used in the treatment of DPNP.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
